Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Upload Failures
Problem: Collection upload fails with authentication error.

Solution:

# Verify API token
curl -H "Authorization: Token your-api-token" http://localhost/api/automation-hub/v3/collections/

# Check token permissions in hub admin panel
Issue 2: Collection Build Errors
Problem: ansible-galaxy collection build fails.

Solution:

# Validate galaxy.yml syntax
python3 -c "import yaml; yaml.safe_load(open('galaxy.yml'))"

# Check for required files
ls -la README.md galaxy.yml
Issue 3: Hub Service Issues
Problem: Private Automation Hub service not responding.

Solution:

# Restart hub services
sudo systemctl restart automation-hub
sudo systemctl restart nginx

# Check service logs
sudo journalctl -u automation-hub --no-pager -l
Best Practices
Collection Development
• Use semantic versioning for collection versions • Include comprehensive documentation in README files • Test collections thoroughly before uploading • Use meaningful tags and descriptions for discoverability

Hub Management
• Regularly backup hub data and configurations • Monitor storage usage and clean up old versions • Implement proper access controls and permissions • Keep hub software updated with latest patches

Security Considerations
• Use strong authentication tokens • Implement role-based access control • Regularly audit user permissions • Enable HTTPS for production deployments

